## Validation Reference

### Validation Objective

Demonstrate that the environmental perception capability enables the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) to establish reliable awareness of its operating environment for adaptive vehicle intelligence.

---

### Validation Method

Validation shall be performed through one or more of the following methods:

| Method | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| Operational Evaluation | Assess perception capability under representative operating conditions. |
| Scenario-Based Assessment | Demonstrate perception across diverse environmental, vehicle, human, and operational scenarios. |
| Stakeholder Acceptance | Confirm that the delivered perception capability satisfies approved engineering and operational expectations. |

---

### Validation Reference

Detailed validation plans, operational scenarios, and acceptance records shall be maintained within the AVIA Validation domain and referenced from this objective.

---

### Validation Success Criteria

Validation shall demonstrate that the system:

- Maintains awareness of relevant operating conditions.
- Supplies reliable observations that support downstream interpretation.
- Performs perception consistently across representative operating scenarios.
- Fulfills the engineering intent defined by SO-F-002.

---

### Validation Status

Not Yet Validated

